Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Observers", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An observer is a saturated chain, its positions the ticks of a clock. Two \
observers exchange light: the message relation sends a tick of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c69c08d5-75c2-4552-ad73-e3790ac29541"],
 " to the ticks of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a04976f-9643-40ce-86bd-e9f40f36b11b"],
 " it reaches by a light ray, and the echo relation returns the message to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3155f59d-3264-492b-aa90-e25988a58fd5"],
 ". A single-valued selection of the relation that preserves the tick order \
is a message function in the sense of Ehlers, Pirani and Schild (axiom D1); \
the message and echo heads are read for their relation, their graph and the \
number of such functions, and their random samplers draw one. The radar chart \
of an observer assigns to every event in its radar domain the emission tick \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76774b31-a21d-42e7-b2e8-9b6e8a273f29"],
 " of the latest tick that can signal the event and the reception tick ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09a224cc-9705-420e-8f15-3132aa2c9bbf"],
 " of the earliest tick the event can signal, hence the radar time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "760bf003-7cba-45d9-8d4b-31b7292086e5"],
 " and the radar distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6697174-9c91-4849-aa09-fc8a3c450efd"],
 "; a list of observers joins their charts. The observer space is the causal \
graph fibered over the chart: the \"Fibration\" reading hands InfraGeometry \
an ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraFibration"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93c18d3d-076b-4df0-9d5b-5d5bed96e3ae"],
 " whose fibers are the events an observer cannot tell apart, on which \
sections, connections and holonomy are read with the Infra Fiber Bundles \
guide."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

